			"File": [
				"⣿⣿⣿⣿⣿",
				95,
				101
			],
			"Message": "build(Output): Remove compiled JavaScript configuration artifacts\n\nDelete all compiled .js and .js.map files from the Configuration directory. These represent the transpiled output of TypeScript build configuration sources that have been moved to or consolidated under a different source location.\n\nThe removed files include ESBuild configurations (CodeEditorLand, Microsoft/VSCode, Exclude modules), plugin modules (Apply, Copy, Transform, Type), polyfills (ChildProcess, FileProtocol, FileSystem, IPCRenderer, NativeModule, Process, SharedProcess), services (DevLog, TauriMainProcess, Trace), and tsconfig JSON files.\n\nThis cleanup eliminates redundant build artifacts from the Output element, leaving only the TypeScript source files for the configuration system.",
			"SHA": "461fcef32466f6afee5de65bf15049c0971506ec"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-22T18:19:24Z",
			"File": [
				"⡿⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				213,
				37
			],
			"Message": "docs(Output): Document CopyNodeModules-StripDanglingSourceMap pairing rationale\n\nAdd rationale to Plugin/Index.ts explaining why the node_modules copy\nand sourcemap strip are expressed as separate plugins with role-scoped\nmatching rather than using the CopyPlugin.AfterCopy hook.\n\nStripDanglingSourceMap's Match is scoped to Role === \"app\" and\nCopyNodeModules writes into the app root, so the transform pass\nnaturally covers every file the copy emits. Leaving AfterCopy unused\nkeeps it available for future siblings (e.g., a copy that produces\nfiles outside the app root and still needs strip).\n\nThis clarifies the architectural decision made in the previous\nextraction commit.",
			"SHA": "fbdf5352b1da3752cc680b5e44fe11c9d3b4a7f2"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-22T17:25:29Z",
			"File": [
				"⡇⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				174,
				19
			],
			"Message": "feat(Output): Extract Sky's inline build plugins into reusable module\n\nMove all copy and transform plugins previously inlined in Sky's `astro.config.ts` into a dedicated `Plugin` module under Output. This enables reuse across Sky, future desktop shells, and test harnesses without esbuild dependencies.\n\nNew plugins added:\n- Copy: CopyVSOutput, CopyVSRootFiles, SupplementFromDependency, CopyWorker, CopyNodeModules, StubUnpublishedAddons, CopyTauriMainProcessService\n- Transform: StripCSSImport, InjectNameShim, ReplaceElectronIPCService, ReplaceSharedProcess, StaticToDynamicImport, StripDanglingSourceMap, ExtensionScannerIPC\n\nThe Apply.ts runner walks roots, executes copy plugins then transform plugins, and provides a BuildPipeline factory matching Sky's ordered Steps 1-14. Type.ts defines the Plugin contract with TransformPlugin and CopyPlugin shapes.\n\nThis extraction maintains the same behavior while making the logic portable and testable.",
			"SHA": "4c879094fd169c2fdf5dc0164e818a4e95f08769"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-22T17:11:26Z",
			"File": [
				"⡏⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				153,
				21
			],
			"Message": "feat(Output): Route colon-prefixed Tauri commands through MountainIPCInvoke\n\nThe polyfill modules (ChildProcessPolyfill, FileProtocolShim, FileSystemPolyfill, IPCRendererShim, NativeModulePolyfill, ProcessPolyfill, SharedProcessProxy) were attempting to invoke commands with colons in the name (e.g., file:read, file:write, shared_process:invoke) directly via Tauri invoke.\n\nHowever, Rust function names cannot contain colons. These commands dispatch through Mountain's single MountainIPCInvoke command, which unwraps the method name and params back into the positional Vec<Value> that internal handlers consume.\n\nUpdate invokeTauri in all polyfills to detect colon-prefixed commands and route them through MountainIPCInvoke. Also update sendTauri in IPCRendererShim to maintain consistency between async and fire-and-forget forms.\n\nThis ensures all polyfills behave consistently with the rest of Wind/Sky/Output.",
			"SHA": "e6a8a93234866009796415ecc121f2d2d226cb7a"
		}
	],
	"TimeStamp": 1780236098102
}